<PageLayout title="Know what belongs to your business."><main id="main" class="resource-main"><a class="text-link" href="/resources/">← Back to resources</a><p class="eyebrow">OWNERSHIP / <Wordmark inline/> JOURNAL</p><h1>Know what belongs to your business.</h1><p>Your website can involve several different accounts. Keeping track of them makes renewals, updates, and handoffs easier.</p><h2>Know the main accounts</h2><ul><li>The domain registrar that manages your website address.</li><li>The hosting provider that serves the site.</li><li>The provider for your business email.</li><li>The content management system used for updates, if there is one.</li><li>Any booking, payment, or other services connected to your site.</li></ul><h2>Agree on responsibilities</h2><p>Record who owns each account, who pays the bills, who can make changes, and how access will be handed over. Keep renewal dates and recovery contacts somewhere private.</p><h2>Plan the handoff</h2><p>Discuss what you will receive: source files, account access, editing instructions, and the agreed support arrangements. Provider access-sharing tools are preferable to passing account passwords around.</p><a class="button" href="/consultation/">Talk through your setup →</a></main></PageLayout>